          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "ADJUSTING VALUES & HIDING PARAMETERS\n\nThe values on nodes can be adjusted by typing in new values, dragging sliders or boxes.\nLife can be made easier by creating input nodes like the drop-down menu and slider in the example below.\n\nAssignment: Set the modifier to Absolute, the octaves to 1 and the density to 22.2 then click and hold the third box of the Phase Offset parameter and drag it up and down.\n\nParameters can be hidden away.\nThis can save a lot of space on your canvas in bigger projects.\nTo hide or unhide a parameter; right click on the node, navigate to the visibility tab and select the parameter.\n\nAssignment: Unhide the Algorithm parameter and change it."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 556.4229125976562,
          "width": 917.8504638671876,
          "x": 1757.7423095703125,
          "y": 390.7598876953125
